; STAGE CODE_WHEEL: anti-piracy code-wheel protection screen.
;
; Gameplay role: shown before INTRO on amiga 1991 and dos 1992. The
; player rotated a paper code-wheel that came with the game and
; entered the matching symbols on screen. NOT present on cartridge
; ports (snes/genesis) or GBA — those use ROM-baked content with no
; protection layer.
;
; Branches that ship CODE_WHEEL:
;   chahi_amiga_1991, dos_1992 (cartridge ports skip this stage).
;
; Structure: 14 folded bodies dominated by palette fades
; (PAL_FADE_*) and resource loads — the actual code-check logic is
; small. Resource 13 holds the wheel imagery.
;
; Unified source for CODE_WHEEL with 14 folded shared bodies.
;
; Folded routines (in byte-address order):
;   INIT_PROGRESS_HASH_VARS  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   LOAD_RESOURCE_13  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   PAL_FADE_DOWN_17_TO_11  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   PAL_FADE_4_TO_18_AND_BACK  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   PAL_FADE_DOWN_1A_TO_4  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   PAL_FADE_DOWN_E_TO_8  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   PAL_FADE_UP_9_TO_F  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   COPY_HERO_VARS_TO_29_2A_2B_2C  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   CLEAR_VAR_22  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   SUM_HASH_VARS_TO_VAR_37  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   MARK_VAR67_AND_KILL  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   INIT_VAR08_TO_178  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   COMPUTE_VAR07_TIMES_44_PLUS_20  (2-arm: amiga, dos)
;   CLEAR_PAGES_1_2_AND_BLIT  (2-arm: amiga, dos)

; Engine-managed special-purpose VM variables (HERO_POS_*, RANDOM_SEED, PAUSE_SLICES, etc.).
;@include "../_common_vars.inc"

; Cross-stage helper EQUs (LABEL_<HEX> / ADDR_AT_* placeholders shared between levels).
;@include "_helpers/_helpers_equ_aliases.inc"

